1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
And now, girls, the news.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Japan is ringing in the Reiwa era,

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,000
but for a handful of people living here in Saga,

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
the return of Fran Shushu is an equally important event.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Camera two.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
So, Miss Four, do you have any comments

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
about getting back to work soon?

8
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Well, I think it's important for us to catch up

9
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
after being away for a solid month.

10
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,000
And Miss Three, what will you girls do

11
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,000
to make up for sitting on your butts, huh?

12
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Well, we already have part-time jobs,

13
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,000
but I'm guessing you want us to do more, don't you?

14
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Exactly! Think you can read my mind?

15
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:39,000
What's next?

16
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Ow! Beats me.

17
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Maybe acting or something?

18
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Or not?

19
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:52,000
I know! Doing stand-up comedy!

20
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Take me, you dummy!

21
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Listen, ladies!

22
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,000
The obvious strat is to broadcast your return

23
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:00,000
to a wide audience

24
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,000
with as much production value as possible!

25
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Bottom line is,

26
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:05,000
television is your only hope to achieve that!

27
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,000
You bunch of brain-dead zombies!

28
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Shut your hold!

29
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,000
You're the one who screwed up, remember?

30
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:18,000
You're in violation of zombie etiquette, you know?

31
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:19,000
Are you ever gonna explain

32
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,000
what that was all about or no?

33
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Look, as the only non-zomb in the room, I'm feeling unsafe here!

34
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,000
I could sue you all!

35
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:26,000
Perhaps I will!

36
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:28,000
So, if you want to avoid uncivil court,

37
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,000
you'd better pull off this big important job

38
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,000
that I landed for you!

39
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Ta-da!

40
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,000
It's a segment to showcase a popular tourist locale.

41
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,000
The beautiful Utoku Inari Shrine!

42
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:42,000
You mean we get to be on TV?

43
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Perhaps your father will have a chance to see you on screen.

44
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Oh, and you're undead wrong if you think that's all.

45
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:51,000
There's going to be another guest at the taping!

46
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:54,000
And that man is the one and only White Ryu!

47
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Huh?

48
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Who is that?

49
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:59,000
White Ryu!

50
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Not only is he a rock star,

51
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,000
he also hosts a radio program called

52
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,000
So Saga Can Be Saga!

53
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,000
The show started in 1992

54
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,000
and still has faithful listeners all over the country!

55
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:12,000
He's Saga's beloved homegrown celebrity!

56
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:15,000
All the answers that you're looking for

57
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:17,000
can always be found here in Saga.

58
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,000
You're talking about THE White Ryu?

59
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:21,000
That's right.

60
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,000
His debut was 30 years ago now,

61
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,000
but he still brings his positive message

62
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:27,000
to the youth of our great nation.

63
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,000
Ah!

64
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Dude, he's the best ever!

65
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:33,000
I had no idea Saga had big celebrities like that.

66
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Moron, I'll kill ya!

67
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:36,000
I'm sorry!

68
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Enough chitchat!

69
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,000
You have to become Saga's next big superstars!

70
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,000
So go rub some rotting elbows with this hot shot!

71
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,000
When are we meeting him?

72
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:48,000
How about now?!

73
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:54,000
If you take a stroll through the shopping district,

74
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,000
you'll end up getting a very nice view of the shrine.

75
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:59,000
We have some handy cue cards here to help you out.

76
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,000
We hope you ladies do a great job!

77
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Thanks!

78
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,000
We're so glad to be here!

79
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:05,000
Huh?

80
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,000
That's weird.

81
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,000
He looks kinda different.

82
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,000
Sorry I'm late.

83
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,000
I felt the wind off Kyogatake,

84
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:40,000
and it spoke to me.

85
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Yeah, this is definitely him!

86
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:45,000
Wow, great.

87
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Uh, hello there, everybody!

88
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,000
It's time for another adventure

89
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
with your favorite pop idols, Fran Shushu!

90
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,000
Today we're visiting the new Toku Inari shrine

91
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:57,000
with none other than the famous singer White Ryu!

92
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,000
Let's see, uh...

93
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:01,000
So, do you come to these things a lot?

94
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:03,000
If that question was meant for me,

95
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:04,000
yes.

96
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:05,000
That said,

97
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:08,000
if you are asking the winds of Saga,

98
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:09,000
then yes!

99
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,000
Hell yeah!

100
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,000
Uh...

101
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,000
Sakura, cue card!

102
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:14,000
Oh!

103
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Oh!

104
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,000
Okay!

105
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Oh, shit!

106
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,000
Uh...

107
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:26,000
These vendors are famous for their one-of-a-kind merchandise.

108
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Every shop on this strip carries signature items.

109
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,000
All right!

110
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,000
Shall we go shopping?

111
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:39,000
What are you looking at?

112
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,000
Some fish?

113
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:41,000
Mudskippers.

114
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,000
Trapped in the society that is their tank.

115
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,000
Held back from the world,

116
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:47,000
just like you girls.

117
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:49,000
Huh?

118
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:51,000
Exactly!

119
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,000
We are like that!

120
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:54,000
I'm gonna set those critters free.

121
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:56,000
How much?

122
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,000
Sorry, they're my pets.

123
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:59,000
But I do have these replicas here.

124
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:01,000
500 yen.

125
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:09,000
Now they're free!

126
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:11,000
Do you think we're gonna get what we need from this?

127
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:13,000
Well, they seem to be having a good time.

128
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,000
It'll work.

129
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:16,000
Wow!

130
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,000
That's such a colorful shrine!

131
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,000
So fancy!

132
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:19,000
Like a dollhouse!

133
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:23,000
Yes, it's quite different from the shrines we had in Yoshiwara.

134
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:28,000
Um, check it out, number four!

135
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,000
Yeah, what's up?

136
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:31,000
That's a shrine to the god of marriage!

137
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:32,000
Let's go look!

138
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:33,000
To what?

139
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,000
I'm not ready for that!

140
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:43,000
Do you think the gods hear prayers from zombies too?

141
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:45,000
Bet they're surprised that we're here.

142
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:51,000
That's it for today!

143
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,000
Thank you for watching!

144
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:53,000
Wait.

145
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,000
It's true.

146
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:58,000
The light does shine on this part of Utoku Inari.

147
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:02,000
But if you let yourself be too dazzled by it,

148
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:06,000
you'll never reach the destination that awaits those who struggle through darkness.

149
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:09,000
What do you mean, man?

150
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:14,000
These days, the glamour of the big city tends to conceal the truth.

151
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,000
If you're willing to crawl toward that truth,

152
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:19,000
then I'll show you the way.

153
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:24,000
To the Inner Temple.

154
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:27,000
He's so deep.

155
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:30,000
Um, the Inner Temple might be kind of the tricky chute.

156
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:31,000
Please let us go!

157
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:32,000
Uh-huh.

158
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:34,000
We're free now, aren't we?

159
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,000
Let's do it!

160
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:37,000
Oh, poopsies.

161
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:43,000
There sure are a lot of steps.

162
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:46,000
This would've been rough when we were still alive.

163
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:49,000
Inner Temple, here we come!

164
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:50,000
Uh-huh.

165
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:51,000
Uh-huh.

166
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:53,000
Uh-huh.

167
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:54,000
Uh-huh.

168
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,000
Uh.

169
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,000
Uh-huh.

170
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:59,000
Oh, wow!

171
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:02,000
There's the Adayake-see!

172
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:04,000
Huh?

173
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

174
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:06,000
Oh, man, you okay?

175
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,000
Uh-huh.

176
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,000
Uh-huh.

177
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:11,000
Uh-huh.

178
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:12,000
Oh...

179
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:18,000
Grasping hold of something that's real is not an easy thing to do.

180
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:23,000
So deep!

181
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:26,000
And that's a wrap!

182
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:28,000
Good job, everyone!

183
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:32,000
Those girls are pros. I don't know how they managed to keep up with that geezer.

184
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:36,000
Right? I have no idea what he's saying, even if I pay attention.

185
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:40,000
Wait, Saki, please don't get angry!

186
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:44,000
Damn!

187
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:47,000
Ryu's words are like fists full of hard wisdom.

188
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:50,000
And to hear them, you gotta listen in here.

189
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:54,000
I gotta go!

190
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:56,000
Saki!

191
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,000
Hey!

192
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:02,000
Um, meeting you today was, uh, really great!

193
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:04,000
Thank you, sir! You're so awesome!

194
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:06,000
We appreciate it.

195
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:10,000
Yeah, we had a nice wind blowing out here.

196
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:15,000
I haven't caught your radio show in a long time, but I'll listen soon!

197
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:17,000
It'll be waiting, kid.

198
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,000
Thanks!

199
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:23,000
But as for me, I won't be on the airwaves much longer.

200
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,000
Huh?

201
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:25,000
Huh?

202
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,000
Winds of change, and all that.

203
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:28,000
Wait!

204
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:29,000
You're kidding me!

205
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:31,000
You can't leave the show!

206
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:33,000
Don't you worry.

207
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:37,000
The answers you're looking for can always be found here in Saga.

208
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:38,000
Saga.

209
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,000
She's been like that ever since we came home.

210
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:02,000
Do you guys think Saki liked that old man?

211
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:03,000
Wait!

212
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:05,000
You don't mean romantically?

213
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:06,000
Wow.

214
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:07,000
I don't know.

215
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,000
It's not that weird, right?

216
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:11,000
Whether you're living or a zombie, the heart beats the same.

217
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,000
The zombie thing's not the issue.

218
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:15,000
We're idols, remember?

219
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:18,000
Idols aren't allowed to like somebody?

220
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:20,000
Isn't that the rule?

221
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:24,000
Well, it does make you more passionate, and I think that can be a good thing.

222
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:25,000
Yeah?

223
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:26,000
You think so?

224
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:29,000
Well, it is a bit of a gray area.

225
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:30,000
How is that?

226
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:31,000
I...

227
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:34,000
I mean, being in a relationship publicly is kind of a big no-no.

228
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:38,000
But even in your day, idols would have secret rendezvous and stuff like that.

229
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,000
So it's okay?

230
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:42,000
Whoa!

231
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:43,000
Did you have a crush on somebody?

232
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:44,000
Of course not!

233
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,000
Don't be silly!

234
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:47,000
Well, I love everybody in the whole wide world!

235
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:50,000
Because everybody in the world loves me, too!

236
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:53,000
That includes me, dearest Lady Lily.

237
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:55,000
Saki will be okay.

238
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:56,000
Just give her space.

239
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:03,000
This one comes from Saga PD's Dirty Harry.

240
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:05,000
Back for more, huh?

241
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:07,000
Good evening, Ryu.

242
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:10,000
My favorite bar just hired this cute new bartender.

243
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:13,000
A classy lady who's got an old-fashioned way about her.

244
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:15,000
She's giving me strong signals.

245
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:17,000
I think maybe she's kind of into me.

246
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:19,000
Enough of that crap.

247
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:20,000
Time for a song.

248
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:23,000
White Ryu with Do You Hate Windy Days.

249
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:25,000
Hey, Saki.

250
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:28,000
Sorry that I got you guys all freaked out.

251
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:33,000
The first time I heard about Ryu, I was a middle schooler.

252
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:38,000
Back then, I used to feel like the whole damn world was out to get me.

253
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:44,000
Teachers, classmates. If I wouldn't take their crap, they made my life worse.

254
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:50,000
So I fought with all I had. Trying to make them see me.

255
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:53,000
And then it happened.

256
00:10:54,000 --> 00:11:08,000
Not knowing where you belong is rough on anyone.

257
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:13,000
But it's times like that you gotta keep your eyes and ears open.

258
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:17,000
One day, you'll find somebody who feels the same way you do.

259
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:20,000
I'm talking to you right now, aren't I?

260
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,000
That means you're not alone.

261
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:26,000
You might forget all about me after tonight.

262
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:32,000
But still, connecting with you over the airways is something I'll remember for life.

263
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:38,000
And the next time you start to feel like you're alone in the world, you'll have this place to come back to.

264
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:41,000
Ah, miss, that's mine.

265
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,000
Eat this!

266
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:57,000
One day, you'll find somebody who feels the same way you do.

267
00:11:57,000 --> 00:12:01,000
Those words are what led me to Reiko.

268
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Then one day, I kicked the bucket and started hanging out with dancing zombies.

269
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:10,000
If it wasn't for Ryu, where would I be now?

270
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:12,000
No.

271
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:15,000
I won't let it end this way.

272
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:21,000
Go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go!

273
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:23,000
Go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go!

274
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:26,000
Ah?

275
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:29,000
Hmm?

276
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:33,000
Whoa! That is so many kinds of illegal!

277
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:36,000
Hey, slow down!

278
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:38,000
Nope!

279
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,000
Writing double!

280
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:40,000
Huh?

281
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:48,000
I'm sorry, but it's an emergency.

282
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:51,160
I'm sorry, but it's an emergency. Please don't lock us up. I'm sorry.

283
00:12:57,920 --> 00:13:00,640
And now for an encore by special request.

284
00:13:01,040 --> 00:13:03,900
I am White Ryo, and here's Do You Hate Windy Days.

285
00:13:07,020 --> 00:13:07,920
Excuse us!

286
00:13:07,920 --> 00:13:08,140
Huh?

287
00:13:08,140 --> 00:13:08,620
Huh?

288
00:13:08,620 --> 00:13:09,060
Huh?

289
00:13:09,060 --> 00:13:09,180
Huh?

290
00:13:15,180 --> 00:13:16,240
Two little kittens.

291
00:13:16,240 --> 00:13:18,620
But they don't look lost at all.

292
00:13:18,620 --> 00:13:22,440
By the way, did you hear Franshushu came back recently?

293
00:13:24,080 --> 00:13:26,700
Of course. I saw they made a post about it.

294
00:13:27,300 --> 00:13:28,940
That's really gross, you know?

295
00:13:31,280 --> 00:13:34,740
Okay. Seems like we got a warm breeze blowing today.

296
00:13:35,400 --> 00:13:36,660
Let's talk to our guests.

297
00:13:37,620 --> 00:13:39,780
We're with Franshushu. I'm number two.

298
00:13:40,620 --> 00:13:43,920
And my name is number one, sir. We're very sorry to barge in like this.

299
00:13:43,920 --> 00:13:47,960
Well, what is it then?

300
00:13:48,340 --> 00:13:50,900
I came here to say I'm not letting you quit the show.

301
00:13:51,580 --> 00:13:54,040
In Saga, people feel lost and alone.

302
00:13:54,880 --> 00:13:56,860
Hell, Saga is lost and alone.

303
00:13:57,020 --> 00:13:58,700
And if you don't do your show anymore,

304
00:13:59,300 --> 00:14:03,200
if you leave, what's going to happen to Saga's burning soul?

305
00:14:03,900 --> 00:14:06,160
Listen, the only reason that I'm an idol today

306
00:14:06,160 --> 00:14:07,920
is because of things you've said.

307
00:14:07,920 --> 00:14:11,420
And there are tons of people like me all over Saga.

308
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:14,320
No, all over Japan, even.

309
00:14:14,860 --> 00:14:17,840
That's why I beg you, do not stop the show.

310
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:20,780
Your listeners need a place to turn to.

311
00:14:21,640 --> 00:14:22,080
Right.

312
00:14:22,500 --> 00:14:25,460
They need a home they can turn to, not this old codger.

313
00:14:25,460 --> 00:14:28,920
You thought I was just going to split?

314
00:14:29,580 --> 00:14:33,080
No, I'd rather leave this place to someone who has the passion to run it.

315
00:14:34,180 --> 00:14:37,380
I mean, hell, even my pompadour is starting to give up the ghost.

316
00:14:37,640 --> 00:14:38,460
Who are you going to...

317
00:14:39,020 --> 00:14:42,580
The answer, kiddo, is always in Saga.

318
00:14:43,340 --> 00:14:43,820
What?

319
00:14:44,660 --> 00:14:46,880
I'm thinking you gals should take over.

320
00:14:46,880 --> 00:14:52,460
Wait, you can't just...

321
00:14:52,460 --> 00:14:53,780
You're here and you're perfect.

322
00:14:54,700 --> 00:14:56,380
So why waste time deciding?

323
00:14:56,940 --> 00:14:57,560
You sure?

324
00:14:58,280 --> 00:15:01,080
You've got the kind of spark that lights a fire in others.

325
00:15:01,700 --> 00:15:03,460
You won't just lead Franshoushu.

326
00:15:03,980 --> 00:15:05,780
You'll be a leader to all of Saga.

327
00:15:09,740 --> 00:15:12,160
I'm Franshoushu's leader number two!

328
00:15:12,160 --> 00:15:15,600
I'm going to honor Ryu by taking over this radio show!

329
00:15:16,880 --> 00:15:21,320
Wow, a heads up would have been preferred, but okay.

330
00:15:21,640 --> 00:15:22,620
This is huge, man.

331
00:15:22,840 --> 00:15:24,800
And if you blink, you'll miss history.

332
00:15:27,340 --> 00:15:30,060
From now on, Saga is in your hands.

333
00:15:32,460 --> 00:15:35,140
So what are you going to do next?

334
00:15:35,820 --> 00:15:40,000
The old wind from Kyogatake is pushing me forward now

335
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:42,780
to tell the world about this place.

336
00:15:46,880 --> 00:15:51,760
Look, Ryu, truth is, I love you, okay?

337
00:15:55,140 --> 00:15:56,300
Don't be stupid.

338
00:15:57,040 --> 00:15:59,880
I'm not the person who truly needs your passion right now.

339
00:16:00,940 --> 00:16:03,520
It's all those wandering souls out there.

340
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:06,060
No, it's Saga who needs you most.

341
00:16:06,060 --> 00:16:08,120
Right.

342
00:16:11,120 --> 00:16:13,700
Look me up after you've grown into fine women.

343
00:16:14,020 --> 00:16:16,260
You're both way too young to be my old lady.

344
00:16:16,260 --> 00:16:34,820
He was really something.

345
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:37,560
That's for sure.

346
00:16:38,440 --> 00:16:40,640
Reiko probably found a cool guy like him.

347
00:16:40,640 --> 00:16:43,020
He said we'd see him again, right?

348
00:16:44,480 --> 00:16:46,620
Not until we grow up, technically.

349
00:16:47,600 --> 00:16:48,180
Oh, true.

350
00:16:49,260 --> 00:16:51,740
Problem is, no matter how many years pass,

351
00:16:52,300 --> 00:16:53,940
we're never going to get older.

352
00:16:54,600 --> 00:16:56,020
Because we're zombies.

353
00:16:59,420 --> 00:17:00,280
That's weird.

354
00:17:00,620 --> 00:17:01,260
I'm crying.

355
00:17:01,260 --> 00:17:06,220
Aw, Saki!

356
00:17:06,780 --> 00:17:08,100
Uh, what should I do?

357
00:17:08,380 --> 00:17:09,000
I'm sorry!

358
00:17:09,520 --> 00:17:10,180
There, there!

359
00:17:12,980 --> 00:17:14,620
I just don't get it, man.

360
00:17:14,620 --> 00:17:41,400
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

361
00:17:41,540 --> 00:17:43,060
What are you crying for, Sakura?

362
00:17:43,060 --> 00:17:44,540
I can't help it!

363
00:17:44,680 --> 00:17:47,200
I'm just sad because you're sad!

364
00:17:47,680 --> 00:17:49,080
Fine, then I'm not sad!

365
00:17:49,320 --> 00:17:50,780
Now stop crying, please!

366
00:17:55,260 --> 00:17:56,440
Aw, gross!

367
00:17:56,500 --> 00:17:57,560
You're drying up!

368
00:17:57,900 --> 00:17:59,700
Zombies aren't supposed to shed tears.

369
00:17:59,920 --> 00:18:01,600
This is how you turn into a mummy!

370
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:06,800
We heard the radio show, and we love you ladies!

371
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:07,920
You can do it!

372
00:18:07,960 --> 00:18:09,120
We're rooting for you!

373
00:18:09,320 --> 00:18:11,380
Since I've been the leader of Franshu Shuu,

374
00:18:11,380 --> 00:18:13,920
I have let my soul burn like a flame!

375
00:18:14,700 --> 00:18:17,340
And from now on, I'm going to let it burn even brighter

376
00:18:17,340 --> 00:18:19,200
and light the way for not just my group,

377
00:18:19,280 --> 00:18:20,160
but all of Saga!

378
00:18:20,680 --> 00:18:23,280
Because then, if anybody feels lost,

379
00:18:23,560 --> 00:18:25,400
my light can show them where to go!

380
00:18:25,820 --> 00:18:29,120
Just like Lakey Mari's lighthouse over at Uda no Saki!

381
00:18:30,160 --> 00:18:31,320
Here's our next song!

382
00:18:32,060 --> 00:18:33,880
It's Do You Hate Windy Days!

383
00:18:33,880 --> 00:18:51,780
Yeah!

384
00:18:51,780 --> 00:18:53,780
Oh

385
00:19:21,780 --> 00:19:25,780
That's how I can become myself

386
00:19:25,780 --> 00:19:31,780
The wind's strong, I don't like it

387
00:19:31,780 --> 00:19:35,780
It's not like this, it's not like this

388
00:19:35,780 --> 00:19:37,780
It's not like this

389
00:19:37,780 --> 00:19:43,780
Love, love, love

390
00:19:43,780 --> 00:19:47,780
I want to be with you

391
00:19:51,780 --> 00:19:55,780
So Saga can be Saga with Front Shushu

392
00:19:55,780 --> 00:19:57,780
So if you're ever feeling lost or alone

393
00:19:57,780 --> 00:19:59,780
You can come to us, we're here

394
00:20:15,780 --> 00:20:17,780
And remember, the answers you're looking for

395
00:20:17,780 --> 00:20:19,780
Can always be found here in Saga

396
00:20:21,780 --> 00:20:23,780
Yay!

397
00:20:28,780 --> 00:20:29,780
Saki here

398
00:20:29,780 --> 00:20:32,780
I swear, I'll light the way with Saga's burning soul

399
00:20:32,780 --> 00:20:33,780
We're gonna crush it

400
00:20:33,780 --> 00:20:36,780
Next time, Zombieland Saga Revenge Episode 3

401
00:20:36,780 --> 00:20:38,780
The Acoustic Saga of Love and Youth

402
00:20:38,780 --> 00:20:40,780
Be there!

